# Build context exclusions.
#
# THERE WAS NO .dockerignore ANYWHERE, and the consequences were worse than slow.
#
# 1. SECRETS. `apps/web/Dockerfile`'s builder stage runs `COPY . .`, so every .env in
#    the repo — including apps/api/.env with a live Resend API key — was being copied
#    into an image layer. The runner stage does not carry it forward, but the BUILDER
#    layer does, and a builder layer that reaches a registry or a shared cache is a
#    leaked secret. `docker history` shows it; deleting the file in a later layer does
#    not remove it.
#
# 2. SIZE. The context measured 1.1 GB and was still climbing: node_modules, .next,
#    .git, and llm/outputs (model checkpoints). Every one of those is either rebuilt
#    inside the image or irrelevant to it.
#
# Ordered most-important-first rather than alphabetically, because the first block is
# the one that must never be relaxed.

# ── secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.docker
*.pem
*.key

# ── version control and tooling state ────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
.venv
venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache

# ── dependencies and build output, all regenerated inside the image ──────────
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
.turbo
**/.turbo
dist
build

# ── model weights, checkpoints and datasets ──────────────────────────────────
# Tens of gigabytes, and the API image loads them from a mounted volume rather than
# from its own filesystem.
llm/outputs
llm/data
**/*.safetensors
**/*.gguf
**/*.bin
**/*.pt
**/checkpoint-*

# ── data and local artefacts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
warehouse
*.parquet
*.jsonl
!llm/configs/*.jsonl
scripts/memory_audit/out_*.jsonl

# ── docs and editor noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.md
!README.md
.vscode
.idea
